From 4350d37c5ba7aaa9dfaa91261f57e1aae1fd49da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "yanyuan.qin" <zhengsheng1997@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 01:00:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [GLM] Give the NextN draft its own shared-experts-fusion
 architecture name

The loader rewrites a GLM DSA draft's architecture string to
"GlmMoeDsaForCausalLMNextN" (model_config.py). GlmMoeDsaForCausalLMNextN did
not override fused_shared_experts_architecture, so it inherited
DeepseekV3ForCausalLMNextN's value and the comparison in
shared_experts_fusion_disable_reason could never match. The draft model
silently loses the fusion the target gets.

The two siblings already do this: DeepseekV3ForCausalLMNextN sets it with the
comment "The draft checkpoint reports the NextN architecture name", and
GlmMoeDsaForCausalLM sets its own. The base class comment names GLM's DSA
variant as a case that has to override. This one was missed.

Not ROCm-specific. The comparison is a string compare that runs before any
device or capability check, and the quantization guard ahead of it keys on a
method only QuarkConfig defines, so an FP8 checkpoint reaches the same branch.
test/registered/models_e2e/test_dsa_glm52_tp_mtp.py is registered for CUDA CI
on 8-gpu-h200 with GLM-5.2-FP8 and MTP, and takes this path.

Observed on GLM-5.2-MXFP4, MI355X, TP4/EP1: the log goes from "Config does not
support fused shared expert(s)" to "Shared experts fusion optimization
enabled", and the draft layer stops running a second, unfused MoE shape --
(256, 8) bf16 alongside the target's (257, 9) -- leaving only the fused one.

This is a correctness-of-configuration fix, not a speedup. Paired against the
same branch without it at conc=4, ITL ratio p50 is 0.997 over 79 requests,
which is noise: the draft layer's separate shared-expert MLP is already inside
the draft CUDA graph, so removing ~5 launches per draft step does not surface.
Acceptance length is unchanged at 3.62 vs 3.60.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 python/sglang/srt/models/glm4_moe.py | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/python/sglang/srt/models/glm4_moe.py b/python/sglang/srt/models/glm4_moe.py
index a4aa494c76ad..fa1f6da955ef 100644
--- a/python/sglang/srt/models/glm4_moe.py
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/models/glm4_moe.py
@@ -1449,6 +1449,10 @@ class GlmMoeDsaForCausalLM(DeepseekV2ForCausalLM):
 
 
 class GlmMoeDsaForCausalLMNextN(DeepseekV3ForCausalLMNextN):
+    # The loader rewrites the draft arch to this name, so the inherited
+    # DeepseekV3 value would never match and silently disable fusion.
+    fused_shared_experts_architecture = "GlmMoeDsaForCausalLMNextN"
+
     # GLM-5.2's MTP layer index differs from DeepSeek's (61), so the inherited
     # substr mapping would wrongly rewrite GLM's real layer-61 weights.
     # exclude_layers remapping for the MTP layer is handled explicitly in
